# This template needs no env vars for the local flow — the two chains' RPCs and
# the deployed bridge addresses live in bridge.config.json (written by
# `npm run bridge`), and you connect with a browser wallet.
#
# Import avalanche-cli's public EWOQ dev key into your wallet — it's pre-funded
# on both local chains. `npm run bridge` prints it when it finishes; it is also on
# the "ewoq" row of `avalanche blockchain describe br1`. It is not written in
# this file because secret scanners flag committed keys, even public dev ones.
# LOCAL ONLY — never use it on a real network, and never put a real key here.
